===Verb===
{{en-verb|trammels|trammelling|pres_ptc_qual=UK|pres_ptc2=trammeling|pres_ptc2_qual=US|trammelled|past_qual=UK|past2=trammeled|past2_qual=US}}

# To [[entangle]], as in a [[net]].
#* '''1880''' [[w:Dante Gabriel Rosetti|Dante Gabriel Rosetti]], ''Samuel Taylor Coleridge'', lines 9-10
#*: ''the scarce-snatched hours
#*: ''Which deepening pain left to his lordliest powers: —
#*: ''Heaven lost through spider-'''trammelled''' prison-bars.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To confine; to hamper; to shackle.
#* '''1948''', Winston Churchill, ''[[w:The Second World War (book series)|The Second World War]]''
#*: Virtuous motives, '''trammeled''' by inertia and timidity, are no match for armed and resolute wickedness.

